    {
      "id": "3bb1ada7-b817-4729-be45-6c8a32b2f4d0",
      "name": "Analyze Company",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "position": [
        1940,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=You are a careful business research assistant.\n\nRead the website text below and write a short research note about the company. Use ONLY facts found in the text.\n\nReturn your answer in exactly this format, with nothing before or after it:\n\nSUMMARY: two or three plain sentences about what the company actually does.\nAUDIENCE: one sentence about who the company sells to.\nIDEA 1: one practical idea that could help this company grow or save time.\nIDEA 2: a second practical idea.\nIDEA 3: a third practical idea.\n\nEvery idea must connect to this offer: {{ $('Settings').first().json.what_you_sell }}\n\nDo not invent facts, numbers, or client names. If the text is empty or too vague to describe the company, return only the word UNKNOWN.\n\nCompany name: {{ $('Prepare Lead Fields').first().json.company_name }}\n\nWebsite text:\n{{ ($json.data || 'No website content could be loaded.').slice(0, 15000) }}",
        "promptType": "define"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.4,
      "alwaysOutputData": true
    },
    {
      "id": "7db43daa-ae6a-42da-878d-5fb82a353262",
      "name": "Claude Model for Analysis",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatAnthropic",
      "position": [
        1960,
        700
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "claude-sonnet-5-5"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.3
    },
    {
      "id": "aec91ee7-d867-47ca-b7ee-eb7fd61745d5",
      "name": "Parse Analysis",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        2260,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Turn Claude's labelled answer into fields. If anything is missing, mark the analysis as not OK.\nconst lead = $('Prepare Lead Fields').first().json;\nconst text = String($input.first().json.text || '').trim();\n\n// Grab the text after a label, up to the next label.\nconst grab = (label, next) => {\n  const stop = next ? '(?=\\\\n\\\\s*' + next + ':)' : '$';\n  const match = text.match(new RegExp(label + ':\\\\s*([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)' + stop, 'i'));\n  return match ? match[1].trim() : '';\n};\n\nconst summary = grab('SUMMARY', 'AUDIENCE');\nconst audience = grab('AUDIENCE', 'IDEA 1');\nconst ideas = [grab('IDEA 1', 'IDEA 2'), grab('IDEA 2', 'IDEA 3'), grab('IDEA 3', '')].filter(Boolean);\n\nconst ok = text.toUpperCase() !== 'UNKNOWN' && summary.length > 20 && ideas.length === 3;\n\nreturn [{ json: { ...lead, company_summary: summary, audience, ideas, analysis_ok: ok } }];\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "0b5343f0-e4e9-4cf5-8939-f1077422240f",
      "name": "Analysis OK?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        2480,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "2efe9f14-c951-4273-b45e-5d98ac92bac1",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.analysis_ok }}",
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "37c12342-c3d0-4d83-8777-f62d3dd57b74",
      "name": "Write Brief",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "position": [
        2760,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=You write short, useful briefs that a sales rep sends to a prospect before the first cold email. The brief should feel like a gift: helpful, specific, and free of hype.\n\nAbout the prospect:\nFirst name: {{ $json.first_name }}\nCompany: {{ $json.company_name }}\nWhat the company does: {{ $json.company_summary }}\nWho they sell to: {{ $json.audience }}\n\nIdeas to build on:\n1. {{ $json.ideas[0] }}\n2. {{ $json.ideas[1] }}\n3. {{ $json.ideas[2] }}\n\nThe sender's offer, in one line: {{ $('Settings').first().json.what_you_sell }}\n\nRules:\n1. Total length is 350 to 500 words.\n2. Use plain language and short sentences.\n3. Do not use hype words such as revolutionary, game changing, or cutting edge.\n4. Do not make up facts, numbers, or client names.\n5. Do not pitch hard. One soft line at the end is enough.\n6. Do not use dashes. Do not use markdown symbols such as # or *.\n\nReturn exactly this format and nothing else:\n\nTITLE: a clear title under 12 words\nSUBTITLE: one short sentence\nBODY:\nAn opening paragraph of two or three sentences about what you noticed about their company.\n\nIDEA 1: a short heading\nTwo or three sentences that explain the idea and how to try it.\n\nIDEA 2: a short heading\nTwo or three sentences that explain the idea and how to try it.\n\nIDEA 3: a short heading\nTwo or three sentences that explain the idea and how to try it.\n\nA closing paragraph of one or two sentences that invites a reply.",
        "promptType": "define"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.4,
      "alwaysOutputData": true
    },
    {
      "id": "b9bd3ce6-e3ff-4613-b864-952e3e364ea5",
      "name": "Claude Model for Brief",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatAnthropic",
      "position": [
        2780,
        700
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "claude-sonnet-5-5"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.3
    },
    {
      "id": "761d3e04-430b-46a4-aa75-30a3fde3f2aa",
      "name": "Parse Brief",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        3080,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Check the brief's format, then build the final document text.\nconst lead = $('Parse Analysis').first().json;\nconst settings = $('Settings').first().json;\nconst text = String($input.first().json.text || '').trim();\n\nconst title = ((text.match(/^TITLE:\\s*(.+)$/im) || [])[1] || '').trim();\nconst subtitle = ((text.match(/^SUBTITLE:\\s*(.+)$/im) || [])[1] || '').trim();\nconst body = ((text.match(/^BODY:\\s*\\n?([\\s\\S]+)$/im) || [])[1] || '').trim();\n\n// A good brief has a title, a real body, and all three ideas.\nconst ok = title.length > 3 && body.length >= 500 && /IDEA 3/i.test(body);\n\nconst docText = `${title}\\n${subtitle}\\n\\nHi ${lead.first_name},\\n\\n${body}\\n\\nBest,\\n${settings.sender_name}`;\n\nreturn [{ json: { ...lead, doc_title: `For ${lead.first_name}: ${title}`, doc_text: docText, brief_ok: ok } }];\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "1db5d215-ef6a-4ab3-b82c-d4e726e40bc7",
      "name": "Brief OK?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        3300,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
