    {
      "id": "7e8dc8a7-26e5-4c0b-8bfa-e139e3da2285",
      "name": "Step 1 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -60,
        220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1380,
        "height": 620,
        "content": "## 1. Start, load leads, and loop\nClick Execute workflow to start. Settings holds your name, your offer, and max_leads. The sheet node loads leads where Processed is NO. Loop Over Leads then sends one lead at a time through the steps."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "970ae336-b81a-419e-8ff3-bf271d545980",
      "name": "Step 2 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1380,
        220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 620,
        "content": "## 2. Read the company website\nFetch Company Website loads the lead's site. Convert HTML to Text removes the code so Claude can read it. If the site does not load, the lead is marked NO and the workflow moves on."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "69f77954-2d30-4edd-9c84-c53892f77a22",
      "name": "Step 3 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1880,
        220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 620,
        "content": "## 3. Research the company\nAnalyze Company asks Claude for a short summary and three ideas. Parse Analysis turns the answer into fields. Analysis OK? stops weak research here, so you do not pay for a poor brief."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fbab2a2e-4966-4f69-9585-bfed4f80c1f4",
      "name": "Step 4 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2700,
        220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 620,
        "content": "## 4. Write the brief\nWrite Brief asks Claude for a 350 to 500 word brief in plain language. Parse Brief checks the format and adds the greeting and your name. Brief OK? stops anything broken or too short."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "26e67133-f944-49df-ab3e-17e0b910c4fb",
      "name": "Step 5 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3520,
        220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1120,
        "height": 620,
        "content": "## 5. Create the document and add the lead\nCreate Google Doc saves the brief in your Drive folder. Build Result makes the link. If you added a campaign ID, the lead goes to Instantly with the link in the personalization field."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5fda6ee7-355f-4641-9949-21c30e3ca085",
      "name": "Step 6 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4720,
        220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 620,
        "content": "## 6. Save and repeat\nSave Result to Sheet writes the Document Link and sets Processed. YES means done. NO means it failed and will retry next run. DOC ONLY means the document exists but Instantly failed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d92960bf-2017-48d5-95ef-3ef5c57e5005",
      "name": "Overview Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -60,
        -600
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 700,
        "height": 800,
        "content": "## Create a custom idea brief for each lead and add it to your email campaign\nThis workflow makes a short, personal brief for every lead. You send the link in your first cold email.\n\n### How it works\nIt reads leads from your Google Sheet and loads each company's website. Claude researches the company and writes a short brief with three practical ideas. The brief becomes a Google Doc. The link is saved in your sheet and can be added to an Instantly campaign.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add credentials for Google Sheets, Google Drive, and Anthropic. Instantly is optional. For Instantly, use a Header Auth credential with the name Authorization and the value Bearer YOUR_INSTANTLY_KEY.\n2. Choose your sheet and tab in both Google Sheets nodes.\n3. Choose a Drive folder in Create Google Doc. Share that folder as Anyone with the link can view, or your leads cannot open the brief.\n4. Add these columns: first_name, email, company_name, company_website, Document Link, Processed.\n5. Fill in Settings, then type NO in Processed for each lead you want to run.\n6. Click Execute workflow.\n\n### Customization\nEdit the prompt in Write Brief to change the style of the brief."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
